<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  The common part and the calendar of a delivery in the French profile
  (NeTEx France), as the profile's resource.xml: a composite frame of the type
  NETEX_FRANCE holding a general frame NETEX_COMMUN — the operator, a walk
  between two quays stating its duration and one stating its distance alone,
  as most walks of the French deliveries do — and a general frame
  NETEX_CALENDRIER with the day types
  in the three forms the French deliveries write:
  - school days, a validity and days of the week whose assignments list each
    day it runs on: the properties describe, the dates decide;
  - the weekend, a validity and days of the week whose assignments are its
    exceptions: a Sunday taken away, a Friday holiday added;
  - Wednesdays, assigned an operating period that states no day bits.
  Written for netex-rs's tests (MIT OR Apache-2.0); places, lines and times
  are invented.
-->
